sequenceDiagram
  participant Client as API Client
  participant Resource as API Resource
  participant PolicySvc as PolicyService
  participant OPA as OPA Engine
  participant Audit as AuditService

  Client->>Resource: Request with JWT
  Resource->>PolicySvc: decide(policyRequest)

  Note over PolicySvc: Build OPA input from request context
  Note over PolicySvc: tenant_id (from JWT claim)<br/>actor (from JWT sub)<br/>subject (target user)<br/>action (access/read/manage/impersonate/provision)<br/>resource (product slug)<br/>roles (from JWT)<br/>entitlements (from JWT or computed)

  PolicySvc->>OPA: POST /v1/data/identity

  Note over OPA: Evaluate Rego rules
  Note over OPA: 1. Load tenants data<br/>2. Check tenant active<br/>3. Evaluate allow_* rules<br/>4. Evaluate deny rules<br/>5. Determine matched_rule

  OPA-->>PolicySvc: { "result": { "allow": true/false, "deny": [...], "matched_rule": "..." } }

  alt OPA returned allow
    PolicySvc->>Resource: Allow decision
    Resource->>Audit: Log POLICY_EVALUATED event
    Resource->>Client: 200 OK (continue request)
  else OPA returned deny
    PolicySvc->>Resource: Deny decision with reasons
    Resource->>Audit: Log POLICY_DENIED event
    Resource->>Client: 403 Forbidden (with deny reasons)
  else OPA unavailable
    PolicySvc->>PolicySvc: Use local fallback policy
    Note over PolicySvc: Logs warning about OPA fallback
    alt Fallback allows
      PolicySvc->>Resource: Allow decision (fallback)
    else Fallback denies
      PolicySvc->>Resource: Deny decision (fallback)
    end
  end
